{#
~/.gdbinit — load GEF (GDB Enhanced Features) into every gdb session.

Linux only: this file and the gef.py it sources are declared only
in config.linux.toml, so they never deploy on Windows. gef.py is vendored at dotfiles/config/gdb/gef.py, pinned to GEF
release 2024.06 — the LAST release supporting Python 3.6–3.9. Plain `gdb` is
pwndbg's bundled GDB 17 (Python 3.13), but /usr/bin/gdb embeds Python 3.6 (EL8)
or 3.9 (EL9), where GEF 2025.01+ would SyntaxError on load. Provenance + the
don't-bump-past-2024.06 constraint live in its .vendor sidecar.

This is a template ONLY to resolve the absolute home dir — gdb's `source` does not
shell-expand `~`, so we emit the full path. GEF is non-destructive: every native
gdb command still works; it just adds the dashboard/context UI.

The OTHER GDB front-end, pwndbg, is a mise tool (config.linux.toml) whose bin/
also holds its own gdb and gdbserver; mise puts them first on PATH. So plain `gdb`
is pwndbg's GDB 17 with GEF loaded from here, `pwndbg` starts pwndbg (it does NOT
read this file), and /usr/bin/gdb is the system gdb. Vanilla gdb: `gdb -nx`.
-#}
source {{ env.HOME }}/.config/gdb/gef.py
